  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal obligated $2.3B in FY2026 to date across 195 awards, with an average award size of $11.9M. Obligations fell 34.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $1.3B in FY21 to $3.5B in FY25 before landing at $2.3B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.2B, followed by the General Services Administration at $774M and the Department of Homeland Security at $157M. Computer Systems Design Services is CACI Federal’s largest market at $957M, with Engineering Services at $552M and Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $194M. CACI Federal also records activity in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $179M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $185M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations. Award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, when present, are total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are CACI Federal’s largest buyers this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.2B, making the Department of Defense the largest buyer. The General Services Administration obligated $774M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $157M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $130M, and smaller buyers include the Department of the Interior at $24.9M and the Department of Commerce at $1.1M. The Department of Health and Human Services recorded $0 in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does CACI Federal sell to the government?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $957M, followed by Engineering Services at $552M. Investigation and Personal Background Check Services account for $194M, and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services account for $185M. Other significant markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $179M and Other Computer Related Services at $114M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does CACI Federal make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "CACI Federal obligated $2.3B in FY2026 to date. CACI Federal did this across 195 awards, with an average award size of $11.9M, and obligations fell 34.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $1.3B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $2.3B in FY23, $2.8B in FY24, $3.5B in FY25, and $2.3B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from CACI Federal?",
      "a": "CACI Federal’s largest buyers in FY2026 to date are the Department of Defense, the General Services Administration, and the Department of Homeland Security. The Department of Defense obligated $1.2B, the General Services Administration obligated $774M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $157M. Other buying agencies include NASA at $130M, the Department of the Interior at $24.9M, and the Department of Commerce at $1.1M, while the Department of Health and Human Services recorded $0."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does CACI Federal sell to the government?",
      "a": "CACI Federal sells a mix of services dominated by Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services. Computer Systems Design Services account for $957M and Engineering Services account for $552M. CACI Federal also provides Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $194M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $185M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $179M, and Other Computer Related Services at $114M, among other smaller markets."
